---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { pageMeta } from '../data/site';

const meta = pageMeta.about;
---

<BaseLayout title={meta.title} description={meta.description}>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container page-hero__grid">
      <div>
        <h1>A clinical technology company, built around the data.</h1>
        <p class="page-hero__lede">
          SevenHills is an Ontario-incorporated clinical technology company based in Scarborough,
          Toronto. We are building one connected platform for clinical data and delivering
          specialist services across the same lifecycle.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="page-hero__aside">
        <strong>At a glance</strong>
        <ul>
          <li>Product and services in clinical data management</li>
          <li>Incorporated in Ontario on June 13, 2024</li>
          <li>Based in Scarborough, Toronto</li>
          <li>Platform in development</li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container">
      <dl class="facts">
        <div class="fact">
          <dt>Incorporated</dt>
          <dd>Ontario, June 13, 2024</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
          <dt>Based in</dt>
          <dd>Scarborough, Toronto</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
          <dt>Focus</dt>
          <dd>Clinical data and pharma technology</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
          <dt>Stage</dt>
          <dd>Product in development</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container about-intro">
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <div class="about-copy">
        <p>
          SevenHills is a product-based and service-based IT company focused on clinical data
          management and pharma technology. The company was incorporated in Ontario on June 13,
          2024, and works from Scarborough, Toronto.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our work sits between clinical operations, data management, safety, statistics, and
          software. That position is deliberate. The people configuring a study should understand
          how the data will be cleaned, analyzed, and reported, and the software should reflect
          that understanding.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are early stage. The platform is in development, and the service areas on this site
          describe the work we are organized to deliver. We do not present client work, adoption,
          or certifications that do not yet exist.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tint">
    <div class="container about-intro">
      <h2>What we are building, and why</h2>
      <div class="about-copy">
        <p>
          The platform is one end-to-end flow: CRF design, TMF, EDC, clinical data management,
          pharmacovigilance, biostatistics, SAS analysis, and final report generation.
        </p>
        <p>
          The reason is simple. Clinical teams should not have to rebuild the story of a trial
          every time data crosses a system boundary. A field should keep its definition, its
          history, and its evidence as it moves from design to report.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>
            That is the product thesis: one traceable record, with eight connected stages, instead
            of a chain of tools held together by manual handoffs.
          </strong>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Our approach</h2>
        <p>
          The platform is being built for regulated work. That changes how we design, test, and
          describe it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="principles">
        <article class="principle">
          <h3>Product plus services</h3>
          <p>
            The platform and the service team develop together. Service work keeps the product
            close to real study operations, and the product is intended to make delivery more
            consistent.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle">
          <h3>Quality and validation first</h3>
          <p>
            We design with validation in mind: controlled definitions, audit trails, traceability,
            and change control. Validation is a process, not a badge, and we describe the platform
            as in development.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle">
          <h3>One record over many integrations</h3>
          <p>
            Integrations are necessary, but they should not be the place where the meaning of the
            data gets rebuilt. We prefer one traceable record with clear links to external sources.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle">
          <h3>Honest scope</h3>
          <p>
            We will not claim adoption, certifications, or outcomes we cannot show. The site says
            what exists, what is being built, and what remains a plan.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--grey">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="vision">
        <div>
          <h2>The SHCData vision</h2>
          <p>
            SHCData is the parent brand, intentionally broader than clinical data. Over time, the
            same approach to connected, traceable data can extend to other data-driven sectors.
            The website and the product today stay focused on clinical and pharma technology.
          </p>
          <div class="sectors" aria-label="SHCData sectors today and over time">
            <span class="sector sector--now">Clinical data today</span>
            <span class="sector">Telecom, over time</span>
            <span class="sector">Marketing, over time</span>
            <span class="sector">Finance, over time</span>
            <span class="sector">Claims, over time</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Why start with clinical data</h3>
          <p class="vision__note">
            Clinical trials are a demanding place to prove a data model. The work is documented,
            regulated, and reviewed. If one traceable record can hold up from CRF design to a final
            report, the same discipline can support other data-heavy industries later.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    title="A conversation is a good place to start."
    text="If you work in clinical data and want to compare notes on where handoffs break, contact SevenHills directly."
    secondaryLabel="Read about the platform"
    secondaryHref="/platform/"
  />
</BaseLayout>
